# Web (Next.js)

## P0 routes

| Route | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `/` | Landing + upload workspace (resume + JD) |
| `/s/[id]` | Result: poll `GET /sessions/{id}` until terminal status |
| `/privacy` | Privacy / retention copy |

## API client (`web/lib/api.ts`)

- `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE` — default `http://127.0.0.1:8787` (local Python) or Worker URL in preview/prod.
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_PREFIX` — optional prefix (e.g. `/api` when using Worker).
- `SessionStatus`: `pending` | `processing` | `ready` | `failed` — must match server.

Stop polling when status is `ready` or `failed`. Surface `actionError` on failed actions (export/delete/patch).

## UX rules

- Mobile-first; touch targets ≥ 44px.
- Simplified Chinese; honest tone (no overclaiming outcomes).
- Show loading while `processing` (stub is fast; still handle async contract).
- Diff cards: 原文 / 改文 / 依据 / 风险; extra confirm for high risk.
- Match score is secondary, not the hero metric.

## Code

- TypeScript strict; keep types aligned with `server/src/api/schemas.py` / `p0_models.py`.
- App Router; no secrets in client bundle.

## Verification

```bash
cd web && npm ci && NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:8787 npm run build
```

Smoke when wired: upload → `/s/{id}` → accept toggle → export.
